# Relyance Provider

Manage your [Relyance AI](https://www.relyance.ai) integration connections as code:
connect data sources — AWS, Google Cloud, SaaS vendors, or your own APIs — to Relyance,
configure their credentials and scan capabilities, and keep every connection reviewable,
repeatable, and rotated on your schedule.

- **Secrets never touch Terraform state.** Credential fields use Terraform's
  [write-only arguments](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/resources/ephemeral#write-only-arguments):
  they are sent to Relyance and stored in its secret store, never in state or plan files.
- **The catalog is your schema.** The
  [`relyance_integration_vendor`](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/Relyance/relyance/latest/docs/data-sources/integration_vendor)
  data source tells you each vendor's auth methods and fields — including which fields are
  secret — so you never guess field names.
- **Validation at plan time.** Credential configuration is checked against Relyance's
  side-effect-free validation endpoint during `terraform plan` (on by default), so mistakes
  surface before an apply.

Requires Terraform **>= 1.11** (write-only arguments).

